ssignments, unused_parens)]` concerns at crate root (already set) — you can still add `#[allow(...)]` locally if needed.\n32\t\n33\t## Legacy files (zstd_vNN.c)\n34\tThese are self-contained: they define their OWN internal FSE/HUF/ZBUFF code.\n35\tTranslate the WHOLE file into `src/legacy/zstd_vNN.rs`. Internal helper\n36\tfunctions/types stay private to the module. Only the symbols in the provided\n37\tlist get `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`. Note some exported names are prefixed\n38\t`FSEv05_`, `HUFv05_`, `ZBUFFv06_`, etc. — export those exactly as listed.\n39\t\n40\t## Verification\n41\tYour file must compile as part of `cargo build --release`. After writing it,\n42\tadd `pub mod zstd_vNN;` is handled by the coordinator — you only write the .rs.\n43\tDo NOT edit files outside your assigned .rs unless told.\n44\tDo NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ae8EQrACF4QyFqR4q5KNb7","session_id":"d726b7a2-9f1b-40fa-9ece-fa56fda2dd37","uuid":"80efe46a-2287-4f9b-b789-06d3776f41a4","timestamp":"2026-08-05T05:09:51.350Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate zstd_preSplit"}
