, ZSTD_dictAttachPref_e, ZSTD_SequenceFormat_e.\n21\t  Inline helpers (all pub, crate-internal): ZSTD_getSequenceLength, ZSTD_storeSeq, ZSTD_updateRep,\n22\t  ZSTD_noCompressBlock/ZSTD_rleCompressBlock (check names), ZSTD_minGain, ZSTD_literalsCompressionIsDisabled,\n23\t  ZSTD_window_* (hasExtDict, isExtDict, needOverflowCorrection, correctOverflow, enforceMaxDist,\n24\t  updateSlidingWindow/ updateSlidingWindowSpeed, ZSTD_window_init, ZSTD_window_update, ZSTD_getLowestMatchIndex,\n25\t  ZSTD_getLowestPrefixIndex), ZSTD_matchState_dictMode, ZSTD_cParam_withinBounds, ZSTD_selectAddr, etc.\n26\t  Constants: kSearchStrength, HASH_READ_SIZE, ZSTD_DUBT_UNSORTED_MARK, ZSTD_WINDOW_START_INDEX,\n27\t  ZSTD_ROW_HASH_CACHE_SIZE, LDM_BATCH_SIZE, ENTROPY_WORKSPACE_SIZE, TMP_WORKSPACE_SIZE, ZSTD_OPT_SIZE, etc.\n28\t\n29\tCommon layer: crate::common::{error, mem, bits, bitstream, fse, huf_common, allocations, pool, xxhash,\n30\tzstd_internal, zstd_common}. Public types: crate::zstd_h::*.\n31\t\n32\tEntropy encoders are exported C symbols you can CALL:\n33\t- crate::compress::hist (HIST_count_wksp, HIST_countFast_wksp, HIST_count, HIST_add, ...)\n34\t- crate::compress::fse_compress (FSE_compress_usingCTable, FSE_optimalTableLog, FSE_normalizeCount,\n35\t  FSE_writeNCount, FSE_buildCTable_wksp, FSE_NCountWriteBound, FSE_optimalTableLog_internal, ...)\n36\t- crate::compress::huf_compress (HUF_compress1X_repeat, HUF_compress4X_repeat, HUF_compress4X_usingCTable,\n37\t  HUF_optimalTableLog, HUF_writeCTable_wksp, HUF_estimateCompressedSize, HUF_readCTableHeader,\n38\t  HUF_getNbBitsFromCTable, HUF_buildCTable_wksp, ...)\n39\t\n40\tCross-file compress functions: exported as #[unsafe(no_mangle)] where global in C. To call a sibling\n41\tcompress module's function, either `use crate::compress::<mod>::FN` or declare `extern \"C\"`.\n42\tPrefer crate paths for functions with complex private-type signatures within the same cluster —\n43\tbut if the signature uses a type private to the sibling, use extern \"C\" with matching ABI types\n44\tfrom the shared internal module.\n45\t\n46\tBuild config: DYNAMIC_BMI2=0, ZSTD_MULTITHREAD NOT defined (single-thread; zstdmt is a thin wrapper),\n47\tZSTD_TRACE=1 (trace hooks weak/undefined -> treat as no-ops, traceCtx is u64 field), no ASM,\n48\tZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5, no sanitizers. LE 64-bit. Byte-identical output. No stubs. No bug fixes.\n49\tPreserve exact error-check order, wrapping arithmetic, and static-branch folding.\n50\tUse INCREMENTAL writing (Write header + `// __APPEND_HERE__`, Edit repeatedly <350 lines) to avoid timeouts.\n51\tDo NOT edit other files or c_src/. Do NOT add mod declarations (coordinator wires them).\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Ae8EQrACF4QyFqR4q5KNb7","session_id":"d726b7a2-9f1b-40fa-9ece-fa56fda2dd37","uuid":"e660a318-3771-474b-bf91-18692a7e074a","timestamp":"2026-08-05T05:09:52.303Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate zstd_preSplit"}
