{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01U9iDt7EkxvRHrUVRrJeqsb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# dictBuilder cluster contract\n2\t\n3\tRead `AGENT_SPEC.md` first. Build config: ZSTD_MULTITHREAD undefined (single-thread — POOL runs jobs\n4\tsynchronously via crate::common::pool), DYNAMIC_BMI2=0, LE 64-bit.\n5\t\n6\tPublic ZDICT types are in `c_src/src/include/zdict.h`. Define them #[repr(C)] in the module that owns\n7\tthem, OR share via a small `crate::dictBuilder::zdict` types re-export. Coordinator note: to avoid\n8\tduplicate type definitions across cover/fastcover/zdict, define shared ZDICT_params_t,\n9\tZDICT_cover_params_t, ZDICT_fastCover_params_t, ZDICT_legacy_params_t in `zdict.rs` as `pub`, and cover/\n10\tfastcover `use crate::dictBuilder::zdict::*`. COVER_* types (COVER_best_t, COVER_segment_t,\n11\tCOVER_epoch_info_t, COVER_dictSelection_t) are in cover.h — define in `cover.rs` as pub; fastcover uses them.\n12\t\n13\tDependencies available:\n14\t- crate::common::{mem, bits (highbit32), zstd_internal, allocations (malloc/calloc/free/memcpy/memset/qsort),\n15\t  pool (POOL_create/POOL_add/POOL_free/POOL_sizeof/POOL_ctx), error, xxhash (ZSTD_XXH64)}.\n16\t- crate::compress::zstd_compress_internal (ZSTD_hashPtr etc for fastcover; ZSTD_loadCEntropy is in\n17\t  zstd_compress.c — declare extern \"C\").\n18\t- Public compress API (ZSTD_compress2, ZSTD_createCCtx, ZSTD_CCtx_*, ZSTD_compressBound,\n19\t  ZSTD_getErrorName, ZSTD_isError, ZSTD_maxCLevel, ZSTD_minCLevel) — declare extern \"C\" or call via\n20\t  crate::compress::zstd_compress once available. FSE_normalizeCount/writeNCount via crate::compress::fse_compress,\n21\t  HUF via crate::compress::huf_compress.\n22\t\n23\tCross-file symbols are exported #[unsafe(no_mangle)] where global in C — call siblings via extern \"C\" or crate path.\n24\tthreading.h ZSTD_pthread_mutex_t etc: single-thread build makes these no-op types — model COVER_best_t's\n25\tmutex/cond fields as zero-sized/unit placeholders that the (synchronous) POOL path never truly blocks on;\n26\treproduce the C control flow (which, single-threaded, runs jobs inline).\n27\t\n28\tByte-identical output. No stubs. No bug fixes. Preserve error-check order, qsort comparators (use libc qsort\n29\twith extern \"C\" comparator fns for identical ordering), and wrapping arithmetic.\n30\tUse INCREMENTAL writing. Do NOT edit other files or c_src/. Do NOT add mod declarations.\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016bHqTUvnzanybj5XjUQTyg","session_id":"d726b7a2-9f1b-40fa-9ece-fa56fda2dd37","uuid":"1b7c216f-5816-4a57-a853-4b516f9cf323","timestamp":"2026-08-05T05:24:16.530Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate dictBuilder zdict"}
